\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces Main mechanical components of a dual-head acoustic stethoscope, detailing the side profile of the bell and diaphragm chestpiece (left) and the front view of the diaphragm retaining assembly (right). Source: Adapted from IndoSurgicals \cite {indosurgicals2024}.}}{14}{figure.caption.17}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.2}{\ignorespaces Measured frequency response of the Dayton Audio DAEX25FHE-4 structural exciter in dB SPL, featuring the primary mechanical resonance peak within the lower spectrum boundary. Source: Adapted from Dayton Audio \cite {dayton2013daex25fhe}.}}{26}{figure.caption.26}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.3}{\ignorespaces Comparison of typical normalized frequency response curves for an omnidirectional ECM capsule, a standard consumer MEMS microphone, and a compact free-air loudspeaker across the cardiopulmonary auscultation bandwidth. Source: Adapted from Eargle \cite {eargle2004microphone}, Ballou \cite {ballou2015handbook}, and Lewis \cite {lewis2013mems}.}}{27}{figure.caption.28}%
